.TH QFW-DASHBOARD 1 "September 2026" "QFw 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-dashboard \- inspect and operate dashboard capabilities from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.BR status | diagnostics | events
.br
.B qfw-dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.B action
.I action
.RI [ action-options ]
.br
.B qfw-dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.B abort
.I operation-id
.RB [ --identity " " root ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Calls the same typed capabilities used by the QFw Slurm cluster dashboard.
Output is JSON for CI and diagnostics. This command does not render or require
a browser.
.PP
The status record contains Docker, Slurm, QFw service, allocation,
service-plane, version, image, and configuration-fingerprint sources. The
diagnostics record checks MUNGE, clocks, CPU topology, mounts, modules,
directory publication, registration, DVM state, gateway connectivity, and
credential readiness without returning credential data.
.PP
The action command accepts the allow-listed cluster lifecycle, target-aware
service lifecycle, node-drain, and node-resume actions exposed by the
dashboard. Service actions use
.BR service-start ,
.BR service-stop ,
.BR service-restart ,
or
.B service-recover
with a target of
.BR all ,
.BR directory ,
.BR nwqsim ,
.BR iqm ,
or
.BR gateway .
Host and service mutations require
.BR "--identity root" .
.PP
The abort command terminates the process group for a queued or running
administrative operation. It does not cancel a submitted Slurm experiment;
use the dashboard experiment cancellation control for that lifecycle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --cluster-root " path"
Select the QFw-SLURM-Cluster checkout.
.TP
.BI --state-root " path"
Select retained dashboard operation and event state.
.TP
.BI --identity " name"
Run an action as root, user-a, user-b, or user-c.
.TP
.BI --request-id " id"
Supply an idempotency identifier for an action.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qfw-dashboard action service-recover --target nwqsim --identity root
qfw-dashboard abort 5c660fb8-4daf-4a50-a56c-b9f87eed24c8 \
  --identity root
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dashboard-enable (8),
.BR qfw-dashboard-service (8)
